There is a lot to learn from the FAQ, and reading it cover-to-cover will 
be educational, but I'd say it will be most useful after you have 
learned the basics of C - functions, variables, if, while, for, return, 
recursion, a few standard library functions, and pointers. Then you will 
have the terminology to truly understand the FAQ.

If you have a question which isn't answered in the FAQ, then ask over in 
comp.lang.c or alt.comp.lang.learn.c-c++ - though I'd recommend the 
latter as being more newbie-friendly.

