If you already know linux then cygwin won't be too bad.

Finally, some advice:

1) Don't ever say void main(void) because it's wrong. Say int main(void).
2) Don't rely on learning by trial-and-error. A C program which is 
incorrect may still compile and execute fine! (One example is a C 
program which uses void main(void).) You also /need/ a good textbook, 
such as K&R2 mentioned earlier, in order to know when you are writing C 
which is correct.

